3: A2 +8.84, A3 +2.06, A3-A2 -6.78, A3 beats A2 71/240. V3_SHUFFLED: A2 +8.61, A3 +1.59, -7.02.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Sign flips from +1.34 (V2) to -6.78 (V3) when spatial sub-types were added.", "observed_sample_and_power": "240 matchups", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Same 240 matchups; V2 coarse play types; V3 adds spatial sub-types; V3_SHUFFLED re-run (what was shuffled is not documented)."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-012"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-012"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-035", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-035: Relative-structure single-game validation BOS vs OKC", "score": 1.155, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-063 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPA-035", "FAM:SF-APPA-063 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPA-035"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Relative-structure single-game validation BOS vs OKC", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Model's top-ranked play types score above team average in a held-out game.", "observed_result": "BOS rho 0.200, top-3 n/a, bottom-3 1/3; OKC rho 0.543, top-3 2/2, lift +0.308, bottom-3 1/3.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "One game; 5-6 PTs per team with 4-35 possessions.", "observed_sample_and_power": "1 game", "auto_validation_status": "same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPA-035: 'one holdout game 0022400946; spearman of predicted vs actual pt ppp (pt'", "observed_method": "One holdout game 0022400946; Spearman of predicted vs actual PT PPP (PTs >=3 poss); top-3/bottom-3 hits.", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive", "observed_failure_type": "A_unanswerable", "observed_notes": "NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-063"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-024", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-024: Alignment regression: shift toward engine recommendation vs series ORtg", "score": 0.782, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-024 (0.78)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Alignment regression: shift toward engine recommendation vs series ORtg", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Teams whose playoff mix shifted toward the engine's recommended PT have higher series ORtg residuals.", "observed_result": "Pearson r -0.032, CI [-0.283, +0.209]; Spearman -0.067; OLS beta -5.33 (SE 19.64); clean subset r -0.079 (n=54); tuning fold +0.135, holdout -0.125.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "n=68 with CI width ~0.49 on r; doc says sample thin.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=68; 95% CI [-0.283, +0.209]", "auto_validation_status": "same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPA-024: 'ootstrap ci, ols with mix-shift control; provisional tuning/holdout split. pearson r -0.032, ci [-0.283, +0.209]; spearman -0.0'"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-031", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-031: Case studies: alignment with engine mix vs ORtg (+3.3 claim)", "score": 0.776, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-024 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-031", "FAM:SF-APPA-063 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-031"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Case studies: alignment with engine mix vs ORtg (+3.3 claim)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Games where the team mix was closest to the engine recommendation score more after strength adjustment.", "observed_result": "Closest vs most-deviated tercile +3.3 ORtg adjusted (raw +5.2); Spearman rho >0.4 in 62% of games. Cases: GSW-LAL rho 1.00 coachable +28.0 ORtg; MIA-BOS rho 0.80 aligned residual +27.9; NYK-LAL rho 0.80 coachable +25.0;  [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No CI or test reported for +3.3; in-game PT ranking used as rho target shares outcome data; 3 of 6 cases are labeled honest counter-examples; every kernel rec is CUT-heavy."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:BASE_RATE"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF32"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-012", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-012: A4 five-player matchup model vs three-player A3", "score": 0.775, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-012 (0.78)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A4 five-player matchup model vs three-player A3", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Modeling 5 players per team improves equilibrium PPP over 3.", "observed_result": "A4 +1.61 vs A3 +2.06 pts/100; A4-A3 -0.46; A4 beats A3 87/240.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "A4-A3 -0.46 pts/100, no test reported.", "observed_sample_and_power": "240 matchups", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "240 matchups adversarial equilibrium comparison.", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear", "observed_notes": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_confidence": "medium (0.65)", "observed_member_records": "APPA-012"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-011"}, {"rel": "auto_addresses_question", "node": "RQC:RQC-002"}, {"rel": "auto_uses_method", "node": "METH:matched_control"}, {"rel": "auto_uses_dataset", "node": "DS:NBA_play_by_play_possessions_and_reconstructed_lineups"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-063", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-063: Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)", "score": 0.77, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-063 (0.77)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Pre-game PT PPP ranking from training data correlates with actual efficiency ranking in held-out games.", "observed_result": "Median rho +0.539 (IQR +0.245 to +0.750); 62.4% rho>0.4; 88.4% rho>0; 10.5% rho<0. Top-3 median hit 100%; >=2/3 hits 78.9%; median lift +0.4261 PPP; 90.8% positive lift. Bottom-3 median suppression 66.7%. MAE cited in la [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc caveat: top-3 lift partly reflects league-wide high-efficiency PTs (CUT, PUTBACK, TRANSITION); 10.5% of rows the model misleads (rho<0).", "observed_sample_and_power": "908 game-team rows; 454 games"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-035"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF27", "label": "Study family SF27: Linear team+opponent+play_type baseline vs simulation kernel", "score": 0.768, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF27 (0.77)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Linear team+opponent+play_type baseline vs simulation kernel", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "The Monte Carlo simulation kernel predicts margins better than a linear PPP~team+opponent+play_type model.", "observed_result": ["[CHT-004] SPOT_UP PPP 2.83 to 1.16 (fixed); linear margin R = +0.505; kernel Det. R = +0.466 (gap 0.001 vs linear additive R = +0.467); 5/5 perturbation tests.", "[PAP-097] linear Margin R=+0.505, win accuracy 64-68%; deterministic kernel R=+0.466 vs linear +0.467 (gap 0.001) after the multiplicative rewrite; earlier additive kernel compressed variance"], "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": ["[CHT-004] NOT_RECORDED", "[PAP-097] kernel R=+0.466 matches linear +0.467; does not beat the simple model"], "observed_sample_and_power": "[CHT-004] NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.478, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-044 (0.76); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-044"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-062", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-062: L5 baseline comparison: V0/V2/V4/V5 team-aggregate regret", "score": 0.466, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-047 (0.74); FAM:SF-APPA-062 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-047"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "L5 baseline comparison: V0/V2/V4/V5 team-aggregate regret", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Scheme fingerprint (V2), optimizer (V4), and agents (V5) beat a scheme-neutral team PPP baseline on |projected-observed| regret.", "observed_result": "Mean regret: V0_NEUTRAL 0.1072, V0_TEAM 0.1053, V2_TEAM 0.1003, V4 0.1148, V5 0.0979. V2 vs V0_NEUTRAL mean_diff -0.0069 p=0.190. V4 vs V0_NEUTRAL +0.0075 p=0.563 (V4 worse). V5 vs V4 n_diff=15 beat_rate 0.275 / cond 0.7 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "n=40; V2 and full stack vs neutral p>0.05; V4 trends worse than neutral. Only V5 vs V4 on 15 differing pairs is p=0.031.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=40 pairs", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}], "n_results": 10}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
